{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the equation \\(2 \\sin^3 x - 3 \\sin x = -\\frac{3}{2} \\sin 2x\\) in the interval \\(0 \\le x \\le 2\\pi\\), we start by using the double-angle identity for sine, \\(\\sin 2x = 2 \\sin x \\cos x\\). Substituting this into the equation, we get:\n\\[2 \\sin^3 x - 3 \\sin x = -\\frac{3}{2} \\cdot 2 \\sin x \\cos x.\\]\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we have:\n\\[2 \\sin^3 x - 3 \\sin x = -3 \\sin x \\cos x.\\]\nNext, we can factor out \\(\\sin x\\) from both sides of the equation:\n\\[\\sin x (2 \\sin^2 x - 3) = -3 \\sin x \\cos x.\\]\nWe can rearrange this to:\n\\[\\sin x (2 \\sin^2 x - 3 + 3 \\cos x) = 0.\\]\nThis equation gives us two cases to consider:\n1. \\(\\sin x = 0\\),\n2. \\(2 \\sin^2 x - 3 + 3 \\cos x = 0\\).\n\n**Case 1: \\(\\sin x = 0\\).**\nThe solutions to \\(\\sin x = 0\\) in the interval \\(0 \\le x \\le 2\\pi\\) are \\(x = 0, \\pi, 2\\pi\\).\n\n","prefix_end":805,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,23606,17767,17,1124,15940,61,18,856,481,220,18,1124,15940,856,284,481,59,37018,90,18,15170,17,92,1124,15940,220,17,87,57758,304,279,9873,17767,15,1124,273,856,1124,273,220,17,59,2493,59,701,582,1191,553,1667,279,1990,34381,9569,369,57668,11,1124,11520,15940,220,17,87,284,220,17,1124,15940,856,1124,9407,856,59,568,3719,3696,10607,419,1119,279,23606,11,582,633,510,78045,17,1124,15940,61,18,856,481,220,18,1124,15940,856,284,481,59,37018,90,18,15170,17,92,1124,50853,220,17,1124,15940,856,1124,9407,856,7110,921,50,6383,7766,279,1290,24413,3108,11,582,614,510,78045,17,1124,15940,61,18,856,481,220,18,1124,15940,856,284,481,18,1124,15940,856,1124,9407,856,7110,921,5847,11,582,646,8168,700,1124,11520,15940,856,57758,504,2176,11067,315,279,23606,510,59,26056,15940,856,320,17,1124,15940,61,17,856,481,220,18,8,284,481,18,1124,15940,856,1124,9407,856,7110,921,1654,646,55327,844,419,311,510